[{"id":"wadda-68-9-0","words":["verb:wadda"],"options":[{"bs":"žele","en":"they wish"},{"bs":"zar želi?","en":"does he/it wish?"},{"bs":"poželjela je","en":"she/it wished"},{"bs":"poželio je","en":"he/it wished"}],"ref":"68:9","answerWord":"وَدُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/d21008fea631e44114fb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Who would have had thee compromise, that they may compromise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"željeti, voljeti","en":"to wish, to love"},"passage":["وَدُّوا۟","لَوْ","تُدْهِنُ","فَيُدْهِنُونَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"وَدَّ"}},{"id":"wadda-3-69-0","words":["verb:wadda"],"options":[{"bs":"poželjela je","en":"she/it wished"},{"bs":"poželio je","en":"he/it wished"},{"bs":"i poželjeli su","en":"and they wished"},{"bs":"žele","en":"they wish"}],"ref":"3:69","answerWord":"وَدَّت","answerSound":"audio/ff6fce9d86bf7d0c4a42.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"A party of the People of the Scripture long to make you go astray; and they make none to go astray except themselves, but they perceive not.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"željeti, voljeti","en":"to wish, to love"},"passage":["وَدَّت","طَّآئِفَةٌ","مِّنْ","أَهْلِ","ٱلْكِتَٰبِ","لَوْ","يُضِلُّونَكُمْ","وَمَا","يُضِلُّونَ","إِلَّآ","أَنفُسَهُمْ","وَمَا","يَشْعُرُونَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"وَدَّ"}},{"id":"wadda-33-20-7","words":["verb:wadda"],"options":[{"bs":"žele","en":"they wish"},{"bs":"i poželjeli su","en":"and they wished"},{"bs":"poželio je","en":"he/it wished"},{"bs":"poželjela je","en":"she/it wished"}],"ref":"33:20","answerWord":"يَوَدُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/8cedbcb17c0ed8401210.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They hold that the clans have not retired (for good); and if the clans should advance (again), they would fain be in the desert with the wandering Arabs, asking for the news of you; and if they were among you, they would not give battle, save a little.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"željeti, voljeti","en":"to wish, to love"},"passage":["يَحْسَبُونَ","ٱلْأَحْزَابَ","لَمْ","يَذْهَبُوا۟","وَإِن","يَأْتِ","ٱلْأَحْزَابُ","يَوَدُّوا۟","لَوْ","أَنَّهُم","بَادُونَ","فِى","ٱلْأَعْرَابِ","يَسْـَٔلُونَ","عَنْ","أَنۢبَآئِكُمْ","وَلَوْ","كَانُوا۟","فِيكُم","مَّا","قَٰتَلُوٓا۟","إِلَّا","قَلِيلًا"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"وَدَّ"}},{"id":"wadda-60-2-10","words":["verb:wadda"],"options":[{"bs":"i poželjeli su","en":"and they wished"},{"bs":"poželjela je","en":"she/it wished"},{"bs":"žele","en":"they wish"},{"bs":"poželio je","en":"he/it wished"}],"ref":"60:2","answerWord":"وَوَدُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/880e1262dedff3cf17de.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"If they have the upper hand of you, they will be your foes, and will stretch out their hands and their tongues toward you with evil (intent), and they long for you to disbelieve.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"željeti, voljeti","en":"to wish, to love"},"passage":["إِن","يَثْقَفُوكُمْ","يَكُونُوا۟","لَكُمْ","أَعْدَآءً","وَيَبْسُطُوٓا۟","إِلَيْكُمْ","أَيْدِيَهُمْ","وَأَلْسِنَتَهُم","بِٱلسُّوٓءِ","وَوَدُّوا۟","لَوْ","تَكْفُرُونَ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"وَدَّ"}}]